Acknowledgment: HOL Light
=========================

XuGo took inspiration from HOL Light, the theorem prover written by John Harrison
(https://github.com/jrh13/hol-light).

  - The logic is the one HOL Light implements: classical higher-order
    logic over simple types with type variables. The kernel in core/ is
    a new implementation in Go; its primitive inference rules are
    modelled on those of HOL Light's kernel, and the definitions of the
    logical constants in ext/ follow HOL Light's.

  - The corpus in library/proofs/ is written in XuGo's own proof language.
    The construction of the real numbers follows the one in HOL Light.

XuGo has since gone its own way. The names, the statements and the
proofs in this tree are its own, no proof here is required to follow a
HOL Light script, and nothing in XuGo needs HOL Light to build, to run
or to be checked.

Reference: John Harrison, "HOL Light: An Overview", in Theorem Proving
in Higher Order Logics (TPHOLs 2009), LNCS 5674, Springer, 2009.

